(:doc :symbol "asl/tools/mesh/cmd.asl#" :text "Command layer of bin/asl-mesh ported to ASL: argument parsing and help, status, dashboard, static, sweep, cross-examine, telemetry, proposals, propose-fix, apply-fix, bench, transition, validate, selftest, start and stop, with dispatch_hook, log_telemetry_event, record_finding and run_shell_probe. Board state comes from ws/asl/tools/mesh/board. Model traffic goes through curl --config - on stdin; shell commands run through bash -c or /bin/sh -c only for user-supplied command strings. Shards and defects are processed in parallel batches via worker slots in submission order where the original used thread pools. A crash the original raises is printed as its final traceback line and exits 1. Deliberate divergences: apply-fix rejects a :target that is empty, absolute, contains .., or resolves outside the root (in-root symlinks are accepted now; the original writes there), and the daemon banner says Sequential instead of ThreadPool. The exported makeCtx, normalizeRelPath, and resolveFixTarget functions are intentional direct security-test seams used by secContainmentTest to exercise the same production validation path; applyPatch is also called by production dispatch. Internal path helpers remain unexported.")
